 wrong there's a fan  theory brewing that just might shock you  and it goes a little something like this  whatever monster is terrorizing Hawkins  enjoys crowds and might be feeding off  their energy to reopen the upside-down  eleven made it clear that closing the  upside down took a lot of energy which  is why she nearly died from exhaustion  so could it be that an invisible monster  with a huge and spidery shadow is  seeking out crowds to undo her actions  this could explain why the monster made  an appearance during Independence Day as  well as New Year's Day and it could also  shine some light on the episode titled  the birthday although we have little to  no detail about the sixth episode of the  season we can only imagine that  festivities will be cut short for a good  reason it's possible that this spooky  monster is blind as well and that he  uses rats as a means to eavesdrop on the  outside world should this be the case it  would make sense that he's attracted a  larger crowd since loud music and voices  can be heard from a distance but for now  this is all purely theoretical theory  for blue and yellow everything that  comes attached to stranger things has a  creepy vibe to it which is why we're not  surprised that one of its teasers gave  us the heebie-jeebies in this clip we  see what appears to be a live broadcast  of New York's Times Square during the  new year's countdown throughout this  video bouts of green coding flash across  the screen with some questionable words  and sentences attached to it at some  point we even hear what appears to be  Mike shouting eleventh name dedicated  stranger things fans use Morse code to  decipher one of the images which led  them to discover the phrase when blue  and yellow meet in the West this  puzzling sentence has us grasping for  answers in all the wrong places but fans  came to the conclusion that Mike and 11  are tied to these colors in fact 11 is  seen wearing blue in the poster whereas  Mike can be found wearing yellow so what  does this mean for now we're inclined to  believe that the crew will be taking a  road trip to the coast where they can  investigate a missing persons case and  since the third episode of the season is  titled the case of the missing lifeguard  we can only imagine that this episode  will touch down on our speculations by  now we all know that the upside-down  isn't a fan of fire but we haven't the  slightest clue how it will fare in the  open waters could it be that an  upside-down creature has found its way  into a body of water where it's  infecting everyone who drinks or swims  in it for now we're inclined to believe  that blue might signify water and yellow  the Sun and since the Sun sets in the  west  perhaps this clue points towards the  horizon theory 5 the countdown the  Deborah brothers were inspired by old  80's movies when creating the stranger  themed series so it's not surprising  that they'll be drawing inspiration from  some of the decades biggest hits  executive producer Shawn Levy empty  towards the 3rd season taking a page  from the Back to the Future film which  first aired in the summer of 1985 and  coincidence or not the third season of  stranger things also takes place during  the very same summer many fans are  inclined to believe that stranger things  will focus on time travel this time  around this could explain why the  seasons teaser took place on New Year's  Eve while the poster proudly showcased  the fourth of July could it be that the  stranger things gained has to travel  through time to stop the mind flare from  settling down on earth if so we can't  wait to see what the timeline has in  store for us  the final episode of the third season is  titled the Battle of Star Court which  makes us believe that the Hawkins mall  will be the focal point of that  time-traveling operation and what better  way to turn back the hands of time then  4:11 to use the malls huge water  fountain as ammo so there you have it  the top